Chia timelord on macOS — Full Disk Access
==========================================

Relevant only for topology local-external. CHIA_ROOT ({{ chia_root }}) and
~/.chia stay on the internal disk. Only the blockchain database directory
({{ chia_darwin_volume_db_dir }}) lives on {{ chia_darwin_db_volume }}.
local-internal and remote-node keep everything on the internal disk and do not
need this grant.

Why
---
LaunchDaemons run outside a user GUI session and have no Transparency, Consent,
and Control (TCC) grants of their own. A job whose program is a script is
attributed to its shebang interpreter. These wrappers use {{ chia_darwin_interpreter }}.
Until that interpreter has Full Disk Access, the full-node job can see that
{{ chia_darwin_db_volume }} is mounted and still fail to read
{{ chia_darwin_volume_db_dir }}. The wrapper then loops on "waiting for
{{ chia_darwin_db_volume }}" and the log's ls= line is "Operation not permitted".
An interactive SSH session can read the same path while launchd cannot. That
mismatch is TCC, not a missing mount.

This narrowing is expected, not yet proven on hardware. Only the full-node
process is expected to need this grant: the interpreter running chia_full_node,
because TCC attributes the script job to its shebang interpreter. Companion
binaries should not need it now that config and wallet data are on the internal
disk.

The wrapper waits on {{ chia_darwin_db_marker }}, which is now the on-volume
database directory rather than a config file. That wait tests whether the
directory is readable. Whether a TCC denial is visible through that test the
same way it was for the old config.yaml file marker is expected, not proven on
hardware. The wait log also includes the failure from /bin/ls.

How to grant it
---------------
1. GUI (this Mac):
   System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Full Disk Access -> add
   {{ chia_darwin_interpreter }} (Cmd-Shift-G if it is hidden) and enable it.
   Then restart the full-node LaunchDaemon
   (launchctl kickstart -k system/<full-node label>).

2. MDM: install the sibling profile
   {{ chia_darwin_pppc_dest }}
   through user-approved MDM or Automated Device Enrollment.
   Opening the .mobileconfig locally does not grant SystemPolicyAllFiles
   on modern macOS.

Do not edit TCC.db. It is SIP-protected, and writing it does not grant
Full Disk Access to launchd jobs.

Scope
-----
The grant is for {{ chia_darwin_interpreter }} itself (identifier path,
code requirement: {{ chia_darwin_pppc_code_requirement }}). Any other
LaunchDaemon that starts through that interpreter can then read protected
files, including external volumes. That is the interpreter the running
deployment uses. This role will not swap in a different interpreter or a
custom Mach-O stub.

Companion binaries
------------------
chia-exporter, chia-healthcheck, and the other companion jobs keep their
CHIA_ROOT on the internal disk and no longer wait for the database volume.
Do not add {{ chia_darwin_companion_bin_dir }} binaries to Full Disk Access for
this layout. config and wallet data are internal now.

This role cannot grant TCC Full Disk Access. It only writes this note and the
profile template. It never runs `profiles`, `tccutil`, or SQL against TCC.db.
